# tier-mentions.allowlist -- Tools/zagent/protocol/TICK.md model-tier ratchet allowlist.
#
# TICK.md is harness-neutral prose: it names no harness, no tool and no
# model. The three MODEL_LADDER tiers (Tools/Vault/cli/legacy-pure/routing.mjs)
# are kept as vocabulary -- `haiku`/`sonnet`/`opus` appear inside DISPATCH's
# `tier:` field and the Vault's own routing data -- but a BARE tier name in
# narrative prose is measured history (a ticket's own routing line, a cost
# note), never an instruction, and each one is listed here deliberately so a
# NEW bare mention does not slip in unnoticed.
#
# One wire key per line; '#'/blank lines ignored. A NEW key not listed here
# fails the gate; a removed mention leaves a stale line (INFO only). Shrink,
# don't grow -- a shrinking mention is prose that stopped citing a tier, not
# a reason to keep the stale line.
#
# Format (one mention per line): narrative:<repo-relative-path>:<line> => <tier>
#
# Regenerate (only when deliberately accepting the current set):
#   Tools/zagent/protocol/tier-mentions.allowlist is hand-maintained -- there
#   is no analyze_code_complexity.py profile for prose. Re-derive with:
#   grep -noiE '\bhaiku\b|\bsonnet\b|\bopus\b' Tools/zagent/protocol/TICK.md
#   and confirm each hit is inside a measured-history sentence, not an
#   instruction, before adding its line here.
narrative:Tools/zagent/protocol/TICK.md:674 => opus
narrative:Tools/zagent/protocol/TICK.md:712 => sonnet
